### **3. Required API contract**

The frontend expects these endpoints. They are contracts to implement or map to your existing API—not confirmation that these routes already exist.

| Method | Endpoint                           | Purpose                                         |
| ------ | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/api/users`                       | Paginated account list, summary and permissions |
| POST   | `/api/users/:id/resend-invitation` | Reissue activation invitation                   |
| POST   | `/api/users/:id/suspend`           | Suspend account                                 |
| POST   | `/api/users/:id/reactivate`        | Reactivate account                              |

The list endpoint should accept:

```
GET /api/users?page=1&pageSize=10&search=kim&category=STUDENT&status=ACTIVE
```

Example response:

```
{
  "items": [],
  "total": 0,
  "page": 1,
  "pageSize": 10,
  "summary": {
    "total": 0,
    "active": 0,
    "pendingActivation": 0,
    "suspended": 0,
    "disabled": 0
  },
  "permissions": [
    "users.registration.create",
    "users.registration.resend_invite",
    "users.account.suspend",
    "users.account.reactivate"
  ]
}
```

### **4. Backend permission requirements**

| Permission                         | Allowed operation             |
| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `users.view`                       | View permitted accounts       |
| `users.registration.create`        | Start manual registration     |
| `users.registration.view`          | View registration records     |
| `users.registration.approve`       | Approve registrations         |
| `users.registration.resend_invite` | Resend invitations            |
| `users.account.suspend`            | Suspend accounts              |
| `users.account.reactivate`         | Reactivate accounts           |
| `users.roles.view`                 | View assigned roles           |
| `users.roles.assign`               | Assign authorised roles       |
| `users.audit.view`                 | View account audit history    |
| `users.export`                     | Export permitted account data |

The API must enforce permissions independently of the UI. It must also enforce campus and department scope, prevent unauthorised privilege escalation, protect the last active Super Admin account, and audit every sensitive action.

